_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcadena/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcadena/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcadena/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcadena/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-07T23:44:14Z","updated_at":"2026-04-07T23:44:14Z","body":"> PR here: [#118290](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118290)\n> \n> > This is probably only missing an enum property\n> \n> Exactly the case!\n\nI had tried this but the change is not reflected in the docs inside the editor. Build the editor, open up a search for the docs, and look for get_euler. Mine still showed old int param. Strangely, if you edit the description in the xml, the change shows up in the inline docs, but I don't see changes to the parameters work the same way.  \n\nI'm trying to figure out how to make the doctool command generate the xml properly in the first place:\nI followed the instructions to generate the xml files and it turns out that for types of `enum class` (see the extra class keyword), which is what EulerOrder is, doesn't add the `\"enum\"` attribute to the xml.  \n\nSee: https://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/documentation/class_reference.html#updating-class-reference-when-working-on-the-engine","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4202852279/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4202874107","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118184#issuecomment-4202874107","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118184","id":4202874107,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc76gsT7","user":{"login":"sxl613","id":32416662,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlc