/api.github.com/users/rcadena","html_url":"https://github.com/rcadena","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcadena/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcadena/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcadena/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcadena/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcadena/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcadena/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcadena/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcadena/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcadena/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-08T00:56:39Z","updated_at":"2026-04-08T00:56:39Z","body":"@sxl613 yeah, the weird thing is inside the editor. \n\nHere is your change to the param node and an additional modification to the description node (TEST: Modified Description).\n<img width=\"690\" height=\"218\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b031ac52-e360-4fc7-bb43-cecac3c0b784\" />\n\nAnd once I build and run the editor, then search for the doc, I get this:\n<img width=\"910\" height=\"411\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5a5a35c9-b296-4e93-aeaf-e7cb2f03250d\" />\n\nAlso, if I run the `--doctool` it replace that line in the Basis.xml file with no enum.  \ndiff with manual changes:\n\n\n<img width=\"898\" height=\"276\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/286e26b7-bda2-4d06-81c6-2c1ac6df965f\" />\n\nDiff after running --doctool\n\n<img width=\"787\" height=\"236\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8ceacfdc-c22b-48a4-b970-79530f5d94db\" />\n\nThough I agree that the generated rst has the enum value.\n\n<img width=\"1184\" height=\"190\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a931c81f-cfda-42a9-b958-31eb31d08364\" />\n\n\nSo, I see two problems (maybe my system only?):\n1. The inline docs *don't* pickup the rst param annotations, they get it from something else?\n2. any use of the doctool on a future change in the cpp classes will overwrite the handwritten xml? \n\nBut, maybe I'm totally off...\n\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4203119461/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4203214470","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118184#issuecomment-4203214470","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118184","id":4203214470,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc76h_aG","user":{"login":"sxl613","id":32416662,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNDE2NjYy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32416662?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sxl613","html_url":"https://github.com/sxl613","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sxl613/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sxl613/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sxl613/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sxl613/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sxl613/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sxl613/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sxl613/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sxl613/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sxl613/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-08T01:29:53Z","updated_at":"2026-04-08T01:29:53Z","body":"You're right -- the `--doctool` does reset it back to pre-change.\nI think this is because of\nhttps://github.